WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:04.892
Now let's compare AND with OR OR means that a record
can

00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:10.152
satisfy any one of several alternatives In this
example we want patients

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:15.796
whose diagnosis is Pneumonia Flu or Asthma Because
these are alternatives OR

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:21.034
makes sense We have a runnable SQL example at the
bottom of

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.670
the slide Try running it in the browser and look at
the

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:29.283
diagnosis column in the result Each returned row
should match at least

00:00:29.309 --> 00:00:34.751
one of the three diagnoses If you are practicing
with pgAdmin use

00:00:34.777 --> 00:00:38.877
the Copy button and paste the query into the Query
Tool Later

00:00:39.044 --> 00:00:42.562
when several alternatives all apply to the same
column we can often

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.789
make the query shorter with an IN condition But
first it is

00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:49.985
useful to understand exactly what the OR statements
are doing
